         packages/apps/Settings gates the GPS source on the feature, not on a
         config boolean). No Settings-specific config_gps boolean exists to
         override; this entry documents the contract. The real hiding is the
         runtime FEATURE_LOCATION_GPS absence. -->

    <!--
      T-THEME-DARK (FR-1) — Dark-theme toggle + scheduling lock in Settings.

      GuardTalkOS is forced to dark-only via the framework overlay
      config_defaultNightMode = 2 (see GuardTalkFrameworkBrandOverlay) plus
      the upstream framework default config_lockDayNightMode = true
      (frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml:890). The lock gates
      UiModeManager.setNightMode(), setNightModeActivated(),
      setCustomNightModeStart/End() behind MODIFY_DAY_NIGHT_MODE
      (signature|privileged|role). com.android.settings does NOT hold that
      permission (verified at
      frameworks/base/data/etc/privapp-permissions-platform.xml:705 — only
      INSTALL_DYNAMIC_SYSTEM, BIND_CELL_BROADCAST_SERVICE, MANAGE_SAFETY_CENTER,
      READ_SAFETY_CENTER_STATUS, SEND_SAFETY_CENTER_UPDATE,
      READ_SYSTEM_GRAMMATICAL_GENDER). Therefore every dark-theme control in
      Settings is functionally inert at runtime:

        - display_settings.xml: dark_ui_mode (DarkUIPreferenceController) →
          setNightModeActivated() → rejected by UiModeManagerService.
        - dark_mode_settings.xml: dark_ui_activated (MainSwitchPreference,
          DarkModeActivationPreferenceController) → setNightModeActivated()
          → rejected.
        - dark_mode_settings.xml: dark_ui_auto_mode (DropDownPreference,
          DarkModeScheduleSelectorController) → setNightMode() → rejected.
        - dark_mode_settings.xml: dark_theme_start_time / dark_theme_end_time
          (DarkModeCustomPreferenceController) → setCustomNightModeStart/End()
          → rejected.

      No Settings resource (bool / config_*) exists to *hide* the toggle
      preference from the layout — Settings does not gate the dark-theme
      preference on a config boolean (verified: DarkUIPreferenceController.
      getAvailabilityStatus() unconditionally returns AVAILABLE; the
      preference is declared statically in display_settings.xml). An RRO can
      only override existing resources, not remove <Preference> elements from
      XML, so the toggle row remains visible. It is cosmetic only: tapping it
      dispatches a setNightModeActivated() call that UiModeManagerService
      silently rejects. This matches FR-1 §11 negative-test intent ("Cannot
      switch to light via Settings") — the user cannot effect a mode change.

      Why no config_show_dark_theme_toggle bool is added here: no such key
      exists in packages/apps/Settings to override (Law 8 determinism — we
      only override framework-defined, documented keys). Adding a fabricated
      key would be a no-op and would misleadingly suggest the toggle is
      hidden when it is not.

      Gap (documented, out of scope for T-THEME-DARK): com.android.shell and
      com.android.systemui both hold MODIFY_DAY_NIGHT_MODE, so the QS dark
      tile (UiModeNightTile) and `adb shell cmd uimode night no` can still
      flip the mode at runtime. Fully locking those paths requires an
      init.rc / system-property gate — explicitly out of scope (no init.rc
      edits per task spec). Tracked for T-BT-FULL / Wave-4.
    -->

</resources>
